# The test-directory -> Component map (Story 2.3, FR-1). Protected Path (AD-16):
# a change lands only with the Maintainer's Code Owner review, which signs off
# every entry. Validate it with `bun run component-map:check`.
#
# Format: one JSON record per Component, sorted by `component`, every array
# sorted; `#` lines are ignored.
#   {"component","tests":[{"path","tags":[]}],"namespaces":[],"classes":[],"aliases":[]}
#
# `component` is a `name` in tools/scaffold/packages.jsonl. A test path is
# relative to conformance/upstream/ and starts with the repository name. It is
# an exact file, a directory prefix ending in `/`, or a name prefix ending in
# `*`. Precedence: a file belongs to its most specific matching entry, an exact
# file first, then the longest prefix. Two entries with the same prefix doubly
# map a file; a file no entry matches is unmapped; an entry that matches no
# test file is stale; an entry overriding one with the same Component and tags
# is redundant. All four fail the check. Tags are `deferred:<item>`.
#
# A Component owns the namespace prefixes in `namespaces` and the exact FQCNs
# in `classes` (an exact class first, then the longest namespace). The shared
# `Illuminate\Support\` namespace belongs to support; collections,
# conditionable, macroable and reflection list their own declarations.
# `aliases` are the container keys the Component's providers bind, plus the
# core aliases no provider binds, owned by their first FQCN.
